# EtKeyboard Component

> **Deprecated.** `EtKeyboard` is the legacy classic keypad, kept only for existing consumers
> (deposit, wallet, CVV, 2FA/OTP, phone). For all new numeric-input flows use the premium,
> value-managed **`EtNumericKeypad`** (`libs/etoro-ui/src/components/input/numeric-keypad/`), which
> owns value state, `min`/`max`, decimal precision, and rejection callbacks. Do not add new
> `EtKeyboard` consumers.

## Purpose

`EtKeyboard` is a UI-kit compound component for numeric input flows that need a custom keypad.

It is designed to support:

- Flexible top and bottom slots via `EtKeyboard.Header` and `EtKeyboard.Actions`
- A built-in keypad via `EtKeyboard.Keys`
- Event callbacks for numeric key presses and delete (backspace) action

## API

### Root

```tsx
<EtKeyboard>
  <EtKeyboard.Header>{/* any content */}</EtKeyboard.Header>
  <EtKeyboard.Keys onKeyPress={handleKeyPress} onClear={handleClear} />
  <EtKeyboard.Actions>{/* any content */}</EtKeyboard.Actions>
</EtKeyboard>
```

### `EtKeyboard.Header`

- Accepts any React content
- Applies spacing below itself before keys

### `EtKeyboard.Keys`

- Renders a 4-row × 3-column keypad (`1 2 3` / `4 5 6` / `7 8 9` / `. 0 C`)
- `onKeyPress` emits pressed value for numeric and dot keys
- `onClear` is called when `C` is pressed — intended for delete-last-character (backspace); consumer controls the exact behaviour
- `onClearAll` (optional) is called when `C` is **long-pressed** (~500 ms default) — intended for a "wipe / clear-all" gesture. When omitted, no long-press handler is attached and C behaves as a plain delete. Triggering long-press suppresses the subsequent `onPress` per React Native `Pressable` semantics
- `haptics` (default `true`) — fires `Haptics.impactAsync(Light)` on every key press, and `Haptics.impactAsync(Medium)` on a long-press clear-all; pass `haptics={false}` to opt out

### `EtKeyboard.Actions`

- Accepts any React content
- Applies spacing above itself after keys

## Notes

- `EtKeyboard` does not hold input value state; parent controls the value.
- `EtKeyboard.Keys` can be used independently when slot wrappers are not needed.

## Dependencies

### External

- `expo-haptics` — haptic feedback on key press
